Redistributed source (vendored in this repo)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

UniVidX — Unified video intrinsic decomposition + matting
  https://github.com/houyuanchen111/UniVidX
  Copyright The UniVidX Authors
  Apache License 2.0

  VENDORED into ./UniVidX/ at commit 382b9002757f4d5f04a90ec23b784dce11d56221.
  Its source IS redistributed with this repo. The Apache 2.0 license text
  is kept at ./UniVidX/LICENSE and those files remain under Apache 2.0;
  only the wrapper around them is GPL v3. Apache 2.0 permits this
  combination.

  Modifications to the vendored copy are listed in ./UniVidX/VENDORED.md,
  as Apache 2.0 §4(b) requires. In summary: the LICENSE file was added
  (the pinned commit predates upstream committing one), the ~12 MB
  assets/ demo directory and the nested .git were removed, and an empty
  src/pipelines/__init__.py was added. No upstream source file is edited
  — the wrapper's behavioural fixes are applied as runtime patches from
  unividx_wrapper_runtime/advanced.py.

  It used to be cloned on first node use instead. That was changed
  because deploys with `rsync --delete` erased the clone while leaving
  its .git behind, and because it removed a network fetch from the
  render path.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Runtime dependencies (NOT redistributed by this repo)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Wan2.1-T2V-14B (Tongyi Wanxiang / Alibaba) — Video diffusion backbone
  https://github.com/Wan-Video/Wan2.1
  Apache License 2.0
  Model weights (~57 GB) downloaded from huggingface.co/Wan-AI/Wan2.1-T2V-14B
  by the wrapper on first node use. The Wan2.1-VACE-14B and
  Wan2.1-I2V-14B variants are NOT compatible with UniVidX — the
  loader rejects them.

UniVidX checkpoint weights (intrinsic + alpha variants)
  https://huggingface.co/houyuanchen/UniVidX
  Downloaded from HuggingFace on first node use. ~0.8 GB per variant.

SageAttention (optional)
  Selected via the loader's attention_backend widget. The wrapper
  replaces UniVidX's hardcoded-SDPA attention with a dispatcher that can
  route to SageAttention or FlashAttention-2 when either is importable.

FlashAttention-2 (optional)
  https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention
  BSD 3-Clause. Used by the same dispatcher; preferred by the `auto`
  attention_backend setting when importable.

ComfyUI-WanVideoWrapper (reference only, no code copied)
  https://github.com/kijai/ComfyUI-WanVideoWrapper — Apache License 2.0
  Its context_windows implementation and WanVideoContextOptions node
  informed this pack's context-window defaults (81-frame windows, 16
  frames of overlap) and the options-node UX. No source was copied.
